- **Hold-Time**: Set to `120` seconds (default is `90`). This extends the time BGP waits for keepalives/updates before declaring the session down.
- **Minimum Hold-Time**: Set to `120` seconds via `min 120`. This forces peers to accept the higher hold-time value during negotiation.
- **Keepalive**: No explicit change needed (default `30` seconds). The ratio remains valid as `120 >= 3 × 30`.

### Why This Works:
- The higher hold-time (`120` seconds) allows a 30-second grace period beyond the default (`90` seconds) for link recovery or path redundancy to kick in.
- Forcing `min 120` ensures neighbors use the extended timer, preventing negotiation down to lower values.

> **Note**: Both BGP peers must support the increased hold-time. Coordinate with neighbors before applying. Test changes during maintenance windows.
