2. Replace `<NEIGHBOR_IP>` with the specific neighbor's IP address if applying per neighbor.
3. This configuration stops the route reflector from re-advertising routes back to the originating client while still allowing propagation to other neighbors.
4. Ensure the affected neighbors are configured as route reflector clients (using the `cluster` command at the group/neighbor level).
