            stale-routes-time 300
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `stale-routes-time 300` maintains withdrawn routes for 300 seconds (5 minutes) after a BGP peer initiates graceful restart, preventing immediate route flapping during brief peer outages.  
- Routes are automatically cleared after 300 seconds to avoid retaining outdated information indefinitely.  

**Note:**  
- Ensure BGP graceful restart is enabled (default behavior in most implementations).  
- This configuration applies globally to all BGP peers. To target specific neighbors or groups, apply the command under `group` or `neighbor` contexts instead of the global `graceful-restart` section.
